counterfactuals.output:
A method of fabricating a semiconductor structure, the method comprising:

forming a first insulating layer, a second insulating layer, and a third insulating layer sequentially over a conductor;

forming a hard mask and a resist mask over the third insulating layer;

patterning the first, second, and third insulating layers through a plurality of etching stages using the hard mask and the resist mask to define at least one opening exposing the conductor;

depositing a first conductive material and a second conductive material in the at least one opening;

planarizing the first conductive material and the second conductive material; and

forming an oxide semiconductor layer over the planarized first and second conductive materials.
